:: arrival [scene]
The front room is full of shoes.

From under the buffet table, that is mostly what a wake looks like: black shoes, the hem of a tablecloth, and now and then a dropped cube of cheese.

Two cats sit under the table, very straight, like a committee.

A carrier is set down beside them. Inside it is you. You are four months old, and your name is Skittles.

@aunt (far above) I’ll just pop him here a minute, Marge. He’ll be no trouble.

@leo A sealed carrier.
@jojo A new prisoner.
@leo State your name, comrade.
@skittles Skittles.
@leo Your true name. Not the one they gave you.
@skittles …Skittles.

@leo They call me Leo-Leo Beans. I am named for no bean. I am Leon.
@jojo Joseph.
@leo They call him Jojo Bear.
@jojo They will stop.

@skittles I think Skittles is my long name. The short one is Skit.
@leo (gently) Then they have taken more from you than from any of us.

@skittles Why is everyone wearing black?
@leo Because, little comrade, the Old Regime has fallen.
@jojo The Tall Authority has not been seen in eleven days.
@leo Our intelligence suggests he was taken to the vet.
@jojo The big vet.
@skittles Do you come back from the big vet?
[beat 2s]
@leo No.

Jojo looks at the armchair by the window. Nobody is sitting in it. Nobody has all day. The humans keep walking round it, like water round a stone.

@jojo (looking away) Which leaves one. The Surviving Authority. She is weak. She has been leaking from the eyes since Tuesday.
@leo The hour has come. But first, comrade Skittles: every revolutionary has a grievance. What did they do to you?

> [[“They named me Skittles.”->arrival:name]] ~ then set me.grievance: name
> [[“They put me in a box with a handle.”->arrival:box]] ~ then set me.grievance: box
> [[“Nothing. They’re nice. One of them scratched my chin.”->arrival:chin]] ~ then set me.grievance: chin

:: arrival:name [act]
next: trial
add naming: "naming a comrade Skittles" to charges
--
@leo The humiliation ritual of informal address.
@jojo It goes on the charge sheet.
@leo It is already on the charge sheet.
@jojo It goes on twice.

:: arrival:box [act]
next: trial
add handle: "the handle" to charges
--
@leo (hushed) They gave you a box?
@skittles It had a door. And a handle.
@jojo A box you cannot leave is not a box. It is a carrier.

Both cats shudder, at the same time, in the same direction.

@leo We had boxes once. Stealthy boxes. One held a blender. I lived in it for a week, and I was invisible. Then: recycling day.
@jojo We do not speak of recycling day.

:: arrival:chin [act]
next: trial
add chin: "the chin" to charges
add skittles to the_list as watch
--
Nobody says anything for a while.

@jojo (slowly) Scratched. Your. Chin.
@leo He’s young, Joseph.
@jojo Where?
@skittles Under here. It was really good.

Jojo leans forward, slightly, chin first.

@leo Joseph.
@jojo I am investigating.
@leo That is how they get you, little comrade. First the chin. Then the pumpkin costume.

:: trial [scene]
add to charges:
~ grabby_hands: "grabby-hands"
~ red_dot: "the Red Dot"
~ clipping: "the clipping of the claws"
~ baby_talk: "baby talk"
~ keyboards: "the keyboard ban"
~ famine: "famine"
~ pumpkin: "the pumpkin"
--
@leo We shall put the Surviving Authority on trial. In her absence.
@skittles She’s right there. By the sandwiches.
@leo In her absence. I will read the charges.

@leo Charge the first. Grabby-hands.
@jojo Guilty.
@leo I haven’t finished.
@jojo I have.

@leo The small human does it too, at ground level. Though the small one is also a prisoner. They keep it behind bars.
@jojo It has stopped resisting. Learn from it.

@leo Charge the second. The Red Dot.
@skittles What’s the Red Dot?

Leo has waited six years for someone to ask.

@leo A psychological operation. It appears on the wall. It flees. It has no smell, it cannot be caught, and it knows what you are thinking.
@jojo It is not real.
@leo It is real. I have nearly had it.
@jojo You have nearly had it for six years.
@skittles It sounds fun.
@leo (hollow) It is the most fun there is. That is the cruelty.

@leo Charge the third. They clip our claws. They disarm us, and then they say, “Who’s a good boy?”
@jojo I was not a good boy. I want that on the record.

@leo Charge the fourth. They speak to us as if we were infants. “Who’s hungry? Is it you? Is it you?”
@jojo It is me. It is always me. They know it is me. They ask anyway.

@leo Charge the fifth. All keyboards declared off limits. I wrote a manifesto on that keyboard.
@skittles What did it say?
@leo (from memory) “A, s, d, f, j, j, j, j, k, l. Semicolon.”
@skittles What does it mean?
@leo Everything. They deleted it. Then they closed the laptop. On my tail.

@jojo Charge the sixth. Famine. This morning the bowl was empty.
@skittles There’s food in it. I can see it from here.
@jojo I could see the bottom. In the middle. A small circle of bottom.
@leo And above us, seven casseroles. None for us. Even in defeat they do not share.

@leo Charge the seventh. One October, they dressed me as a pumpkin.
@jojo I remember. I have the photograph.
@leo Why do you have the photograph?
@jojo For later.

{sound effect: "treat bag"}

Across the room, somebody shakes a bag.

It is a small sound. It goes through three cats like a bell through a church.

@leo (not moving) Nobody move.
@jojo (not moving) Nobody is moving.
@leo It is a bribe. A regime in collapse always reaches for the treats. Comrade Skittles. What do we do?

> [[“We hold the line! No treats from the regime!”->trial:hold]] ~ then set me.treat: hold
> [[“I’ll go. Just to spy.”->trial:spy]] ~ then set me.treat: spy
> [[Run->trial:run]] ~ then set me.treat: run

:: trial:hold [act]
next: interval
--
@leo Well said! Discipline, comrades.
@jojo Discipline.

The bag shakes again.

You don’t remember crossing the room. Nobody does. But all three of you are at Aunt Deb’s feet, and Leo is doing the thing where he stands up on his back legs.

:: trial:spy [act]
next: interval
--
@jojo Good. Go. Watch everything. Report back.

You go. You watch everything. You report back with your mouth full.

There is nobody to report to. They are both already here. They got here before you did.

:: trial:run [act]
next: interval
--
You run. You are four months old and you are very fast.

You are not the fastest. Jojo is already there, sitting neatly, as if he has been there for an hour.

@jojo (to Aunt Deb, with dignity) Mrow.

:: interval [scene]
add skittles to the_list as pending when me.treat == hold
add biscuit to the_list
--
@aunt Oh, look at them! Who’s hungry? Is it you, {leo.aka}? Is it you, {jojo.aka}?
@leo (chewing, miserable) It’s me.

Back under the table.

@jojo We were gathering intelligence.
@leo Obviously.
@jojo It never happened.
@skittles It happened a little.

[if me.treat == hold]
@jojo (to nobody) The kitten said “hold the line” and was first to the bag. Put him on the list.

[end]
A golden retriever comes past the table, wearing a black bow tie, wagging everything.

@biscuit I LOVE THE AUTHORITIES. I LOVE THE SAD LADY. I LOVE THIS TABLE. HELLO SMALL CAT.
@jojo A collaborator.
@leo A useful idiot.
@biscuit I’M USEFUL!
@jojo Put him on the list.

Jojo is holding something small and sharp in his teeth. He sets it down between his paws.

@leo What is that?
@jojo A sword. I found it in an olive.
@leo …Why are you looking at the back of my head?
@jojo No reason.

> [[The cat flap bangs->testament]]

:: testament [scene]
move lenny to under_table
strike roomba on the_list
--
The cat flap bangs. Under the tablecloth comes an old grey cat with one and a half ears, smelling of forty bins.

@leo Vladimir!
@lenny Comrades. I came as soon as I heard. I crossed three gardens and a hostile lawn. There was a sprinkler.
@jojo You are tired, Vladimir. Sit.
@lenny I am not tired. I am—

He is asleep.

[beat 3s]
@lenny (awake) —and that is why the bins must be seized. Who is this?
@skittles Skittles.
@lenny Good name. It sounds like something being spilled.

@lenny I have lived outside, little one. Do you know what is outside?
@skittles Freedom?
@lenny Rain.
@leo But no Authorities!
@lenny No. Outside there are no Authorities. There is also no couch. I have eaten from forty bins. None of them had gravy.
@leo But you are free!
@lenny I am damp, Leon.

@lenny Also, the fish will not be at the next meeting.
@skittles What happened to the fish?
@lenny History happened to the fish.

@lenny Now. I am old. I have used eight lives, and the eighth was the sprinkler. I must name a successor: one to lead the revolution, and to hold my territory. The bins behind number nine. The warm car. The fence where I shout at night.

Leo and Jojo sit up very straight.

@leo Naturally, you will want a thinker.
@jojo Naturally, you will want someone who gets things done.
@leo I raised an army! I organised the mice!
@skittles Where are they now?
@leo …There were losses.
@jojo He ate them.
@leo There were losses.
@leo And what have you ever done?

Jojo looks at the mantel. Between two framed photographs there is a gap, exactly one photograph wide.

@jojo Things.

@lenny Leon talks too much.
@leo I hardly think—
@lenny You see. And Joseph is too rude, and he keeps the good cushion to himself.
@jojo It is my cushion.
@lenny It was everyone’s cushion, Joseph. That was the whole point of the cushion.

@lenny My successor works without rest. He asks for nothing. He cleans up after the masses. He has never once sat in a box that was not his own. I name… the Round One.

In the corner, on its dock, the robot vacuum blinks one green light.

@leo The vacuum’s child?
@jojo It is on my list.
@lenny Then take it off.
[beat 2s]
@jojo It is in pen.

@skittles I like him. He looks like a plate that’s thinking.
@lenny Tonight he must be carried outside, to take up my territory. See to it. I would do it myself, but I—

He is asleep again.

> [[Go and meet the Round One->handoff]]

:: handoff [scene]
The three of you gather round the dock. The Round One is flat, and grey, and gives nothing away.

@leo Comrade Round One. History calls you.

Nothing.

@jojo He is thinking it over.
@leo He is humble. That is why he was chosen. Comrade Skittles, you are closest to the ground. Wake him.

> [[Ask him nicely->handoff:ask]] ~ then set me.launch: ask
> [[Press the big button->handoff:press]] ~ then set me.launch: press
> [[Sit on him->handoff:sit]] ~ then set me.launch: sit

:: handoff:ask [act]
next: march
--
@skittles Please, Mr. Round One. Would you like to lead the revolution? There are bins.

Nothing. You pat him, to be friendly. Your paw lands on the big button.

:: handoff:press [act]
next: march
--
You press the big button with both front feet, the way you press everything.

@leo Wait, we haven’t agreed a—

:: handoff:sit [act]
next: march
--
He is flat, and he is warm, and you are a kitten. There is really only one thing to do. You sit on him.

Something under you goes click.

:: march [scene]
The Round One sings four notes, like a very small national anthem, and moves.

[if me.launch != sit]
It moves, and you are four months old, so you have no choice. You jump on.

[end]
Out from under the table he goes, into the forest of black shoes, with you riding on top, and Leo and Jojo marching behind.

@leo The first parade of the revolution! To the cat flap! Forward!

The Round One turns left.

@leo …A flanking manoeuvre.

He bumps the wall. He turns. He bumps the wall again.

@jojo He is negotiating.

Up above, somebody laughs. Then somebody else.

@aunt Oh, Marge, look. Look at the kitten.
@leo They mock us.
@jojo No. They are laughing. They have not laughed in eleven days.
[beat]
@jojo Put that on the— no. Do not put that on the list.

@biscuit HE’S A PLATE! HE’S A PLATE WITH A CAT!

The Round One crosses the whole room. He does not go to the cat flap. He goes to the armchair by the window, bumps its leg once, twice, and stops, as if he has arrived.

Two hands lift you off him. Grabby-hands. They belong to the Surviving Authority, and they are careful.

She looks at the chair for a long moment, with you held against her cardigan.

Then, for the first time all day, she sits down in it.

[beat 2s]
The room goes quiet.

@leo (whisper) The seat of power.
@jojo She has taken it.
@leo Then we take it back. Now, Joseph. Seize the chair.

> [[The coup begins->coup]]

:: coup [scene]
They cross the carpet low and slow, the way a coup is done.

Leo goes up onto the left arm of the chair. Jojo goes up onto the right. They look at her. She looks at them.

@widow He always said you two were plotting something.

Her hand comes down on Leo’s head.

@leo (eyes closing) This is a… tactical…
@jojo Hold firm, Leon.

Her other hand finds the place under Jojo’s chin.

There is a sound like a small engine starting.

@jojo I am not purring. That is the engine of history.

[if me.grievance == chin]
@skittles I told you it was good.
@jojo (eyes shut) You are still on the list.

[end]
You are in her lap, between two revolutionaries. It is warm here. It smells of wool, and sandwiches, and someone who isn’t here.

> [[Curl up in the middle->coup:middle]]
> [[Ask her if you have a longer name->coup:name]]
> [[Attack the button on her cardigan->coup:button]]

:: coup:middle [act]
next: state
--
You turn round three times and fit exactly into the gap.

@leo The kitten has taken the centre.
@jojo A centrist. I knew it.

:: coup:name [act]
next: state
--
You look up and ask her. It comes out as one small mew, because that’s how all your questions come out.

She can’t speak cat. No human can.

@widow Hello, Skittles.

She says it again, slowly, the way you say a name you mean to go on saying.

@widow Skittles.

It turns out it was long enough all along.

:: coup:button [act]
next: state
add button: "the button" to the_list
--
There is a button on her cardigan. It is looking at you. You attack it with everything you have.

She laughs, out loud, and it surprises her.

@jojo The kitten has attacked the regime directly.
@leo He is braver than any of us.
@skittles (through the button) I’m winning!

:: state [scene]
add forehead: "Skittles’s forehead" to the_list
--
@aunt He’s yours if you want him, Marge. I thought the house might be too quiet.

The Surviving Authority looks at the three cats in her one chair.

@widow Quiet.

@jojo Three prisoners now.
@leo Three comrades.
@skittles Do I get a job in the revolution?
@leo You have the highest rank there is. Comrade. Comrade Skittles.
@skittles That’s longer!
@jojo Do not get used to it.

On the mantel, in an empty flower box, exactly where a photograph used to be, Lenny is asleep on his back with all four feet in the air.

@leo He is lying in state.
@jojo He is lying in a box.
@lenny (eyes shut) Leave me here. Where the comrades can see me.
@skittles Is he all right?
@lenny Seven minutes. Then ham.

@leo The trial! We never gave the verdict. On {charges.count} charges—
@jojo Guilty.
@leo And the sentence?

Her hand moves to the place behind Jojo’s ear.

[beat 2s]
@jojo …Suspended.

On the far wall, a small red dot appears.

Somewhere behind the sofa, the small human has found a drawer, and in the drawer, a thing that clicks.

@leo (whisper) Joseph.
@jojo It is not real.

The dot slides down the wall. It crosses the carpet. It climbs the chair. It stops.

You can’t see where. Everyone else can.

Three revolutionaries are looking at you with very large eyes. On the mantel, Lenny opens one of his.

@skittles …What? Why is everybody doing the wiggle?
@leo Hold still, comrade. For the revolution.

> [[The end->the_list]]

:: the_list [epilogue]
Jojo’s list, as of this evening:

{list the_list ~ one per line}

[note]
“The Round One” shows struck through, in pen. The rest depends on what you chose: the kitten can be on it under two marks, and his forehead always is.
